Finish a download that ended before its decompressor started

A small file (address_parser_postal_codes.dat.bz2, 3 kB) can arrive
before bunzip2 has started. onDownloaded() then returned without closing
the process' input, and the finished signal does not come again: the
download ended in a time-out after a minute (seen on FreeBSD).

diff --git a/server/src/filedownloader.cpp b/server/src/filedownloader.cpp
index 95359e1..187dc88 100644
--- a/server/src/filedownloader.cpp
+++ b/server/src/filedownloader.cpp
@@ -404,6 +404,9 @@ void FileDownloader::onProcessStarted()
 {
   m_process_started = true;
   onNetworkReadyRead(); // pipe all data in that has been collected already
+  // a small file may have been downloaded before the process started:
+  // onDownloaded() returned then, and nothing closes the process' input
+  if (m_reply && m_reply->isFinished()) onDownloaded();
 }
 
 void FileDownloader::onProcessRead()
